*
* START-DESCRIPTION:
*
*   call $tk_run(allow, sentence, out, status, err)
*
*     allow     the commands this tool may run, lower case, separated by spaces: the list the tool declares at its top
*     sentence  the command, built by the tool from values it has checked
*     out       returned: what the command printed
*     status    returned: the command's return code (@system.return.code), 0 when it was not run
*     err       returned: null when the command was run; else the message that says why it was not (12809-12812).  Nothing ran.
*
*   Refused before anything runs: an empty sentence; a first word that is not in allow (so a defect in a tool cannot run sh); a word that holds
*   any character but a-z, 0-9, dot, dash and underscore (so a name or a word cannot carry a second command, a quote, a mark or a control
*   character); a sentence over 40 words or 500 characters.  The first word is compared as typed, in lower case.
*
*   It runs the command with EXECUTE, trapping aborts, so a command that aborts returns here.  The command's own checks, quoting, group handling
*   and audit line are the authority for what it does: this routine writes no audit line and changes nothing itself.  A command that asks a
*   question or a password is not run through here (the tool hands the terminal over for it).
*
* END-DESCRIPTION
*
* START-CODE

$internal
subroutine tk_run(allow, sentence, out, status, err)
$catalog $tk_run

$include tk.h

   err = ''
   out = ''
   status = 0

   s = trim(sentence)
   if s = '' then
      err = sysmsg(12809)
      return
   end

   if len(s) > 500 then
      err = sysmsg(12812)
      return
   end
   nw = dcount(s, ' ')
   if nw > 40 then
      err = sysmsg(12812)
      return
   end

   verb = field(s, ' ', 1)
   ok.verb = @false
   na = dcount(allow, ' ')
   for i = 1 to na
      if field(allow, ' ', i) = verb and verb # '' then ok.verb = @true
   next i
   if not(ok.verb) then
      err = sysmsg(12810, verb)
      return
   end

   good = 'abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz0123456789._-'
   for i = 1 to nw
      w = field(s, ' ', i)
      for j = 1 to len(w)
         if index(good, w[j, 1], 1) = 0 then
            err = sysmsg(12811, w)
            return
         end
      next j
   next i

   execute s trapping aborts capturing out
   status = @system.return.code

   return
end

* END-CODE
